00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:07.560
Moody's recession warning and May CPI pressures are creating caution around consumer

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:13.740
and housing exposure. Canadian investors are being flagged to reassess housing-related assets

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:21.400
after record insolvencies since 2009. Portfolio cumulative returns and alpha versus the NASDAQ

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:28.280
are unavailable in today's tracker data. China's planned $295 billion data center buildout

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:34.960
over five years creates a long cycle infrastructure theme. This spending extends beyond single-stock

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.460
AI exposure. The commitment rewards investors who focus on companies supplying power,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.480
cooling, and networking equipment. Avoid chasing headline chip names in this setup.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:51.580
Pair the approach with volume confirmation above the 20-day average to avoid early fades seen

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:57.940
in prior rotations. Canadian investors can access this through global infrastructure ETFs

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.520
or individual names with verified supply chain exposure.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.880
Stay inside TF's A contribution limits while doing so.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:12.180
Historical parallels show these buildouts deliver the strongest returns in years 2-4

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:18.200
once initial CAP-X peaks. Risks include sudden export control tightening from Taiwan

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:24.240
that could disrupt component flows. Now consider how this long cycle idea contrasts

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:31.780
with real estate exposure many Canadians already hold. Imagine you allocated $50,000 from your TFSA

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:37.660
into a rental property in a mid-sized Canadian city last year. You expected steady cash flow,

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:41.800
but the mortgage payment and maintenance quickly consumed most of the rental income.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:47.880
Capital gains tax treatment on any eventual sale still applies at the new inclusion rate.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:54.260
Publicly traded reads, such as Rio Can or Canadian apartment read, offer the same real estate

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.920
exposure. They provide daily liquidity and no property management burden.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:04.520
Their distributions are taxed as ordinary income inside non-registered accounts.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.340
Mortgage investment corporations provide higher yields through private lending.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:14.460
They carry credit risk that is harder to diversify than a broad REIT ETF.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:21.680
The BRR strategy can be adapted for Canadian markets by using a HELOC on an existing property.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.360
Yet it triggers superficial loss rules if you repurchase the same asset within 30 days.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:33.180
Professionals always compare after tax internal rates of return across REITs,

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.540
MICs, and direct ownership before committing capital.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.980
The biggest mistake with real estate allocation is assuming direct ownership always

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:47.760
outperforms liquid alternatives. Always model the full tax and effort cost of each vehicle

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.440
before choosing. For the practice investment of the day, we are skipping a new position.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:58.240
No qualifying setup meets both fundamental catalyst and volumes by criteria outside the

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:04.620
